  "pages": [
    {
      "cover": true,
      "sentenceId": 0,
      "image": "assets/images/00.webp",
      "audio": "",
      "en": "",
      "cn": ""
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 1,
      "sourceSentenceId": 1,
      "chunkId": "s50-p01",
      "image": "assets/images/01.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s50-p01.mp3",
      "en": "Nature is amazing!",
      "cn": "大自然真是令人惊叹！"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 2,
      "sourceSentenceId": 2,
      "chunkId": "s50-p02",
      "image": "assets/images/02.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s50-p02.mp3",
      "en": "Take a close look at the world of insects, and you'll discover many unbelievable things.",
      "cn": "仔细观察昆虫的世界，你会发现许多不可思议的事情。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 3,
      "sourceSentenceId": 3,
      "chunkId": "s50-p03",
      "image": "assets/images/03.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s50-p03.mp3",
      "en": "Consider butterflies.",
      "cn": "以蝴蝶为例。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 4,
      "sourceSentenceId": 4,
      "chunkId": "s50-p04",
      "image": "assets/images/04.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s50-p04.mp3",
      "en": "They have beautiful, colourful wings, and strong, fantastic flying skills.",
      "cn": "它们拥有美丽多彩的翅膀，还有强大、非凡的飞行技能。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 5,
      "sourceSentenceId": 5,
      "chunkId": "s50-p05",
      "image": "assets/images/05.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s50-p05.mp3",
      "en": "On summer days, you always see them flying freely over gardens and wild fields.",
      "cn": "夏日里，你总能看到它们在花园和野外自由地飞翔。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 6,
      "sourceSentenceId": 6,
      "chunkId": "s50-p06",
      "image": "assets/images/06.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s50-p06.mp3",
      "en": "How a butterfly appears is one of the amazing wonders of nature.",
      "cn": "蝴蝶诞生的过程是大自然令人惊叹的奇迹之一。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 7,
      "sourceSentenceId": 7,
      "chunkId": "s50-p07",
      "image": "assets/images/07.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s50-p07.mp3",
      "en": "In the beginning, female butterflies lay a small egg on a leaf or stem of a plant.",
      "cn": "起初，雌蝶会在植物的叶子或茎上产下一个小巧的卵。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 8,
      "sourceSentenceId": 8,
      "chunkId": "s50-p08",
      "image": "assets/images/08.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s50-p08.mp3",
      "en": "The egg will become something completely different in a few days.",
      "cn": "几天后，这个卵会变成完全不同的东西。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 9,
      "sourceSentenceId": 9,
      "chunkId": "s50-p09",
      "image": "assets/images/09.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s50-p09.mp3",
      "en": "It first becomes a walking insect called caterpillar.",
      "cn": "它首先会变成一种名为毛毛虫的爬行昆虫。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 10,
      "sourceSentenceId": 10,
      "chunkId": "s50-p10",
      "image": "assets/images/10.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s50-p10.mp3",
      "en": "It then has legs, eyes and a body that looks fat.",
      "cn": "接下来它会有腿、眼睛和看起来胖乎乎的身体。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 11,
      "sourceSentenceId": 11,
      "chunkId": "s50-p11",
      "image": "assets/images/11.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s50-p11.mp3",
      "en": "But it is still not a butterfly.",
      "cn": "但它还不是蝴蝶。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 12,
      "sourceSentenceId": 12,
      "chunkId": "s50-p12",
      "image": "assets/images/12.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s50-p12.mp3",
      "en": "Soon, after growing big, the caterpillar produces silk threads to make a cover for itself.",
      "cn": "很快，当毛毛虫长大后，它会吐出丝线为自己做一个外壳。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 13,
      "sourceSentenceId": 13,
      "chunkId": "s50-p13",
      "image": "assets/images/13.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s50-p13.mp3",
      "en": "It covers itself in a nice protective blanket to go to sleep.",
      "cn": "它用这漂亮的保护毯将自己包裹起来，进入休眠状态。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 14,
      "sourceSentenceId": 14,
      "chunkId": "s50-p14",
      "image": "assets/images/14.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s50-p14.mp3",
      "en": "It ties itself to a leaf or a branch, where it is not easy for birds to find.",
      "cn": "它把自己固定在一片叶子或一根枝条上，在那里它不容易被鸟类发现。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 15,
      "sourceSentenceId": 15,
      "chunkId": "s50-p15",
      "image": "assets/images/15.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s50-p15.mp3",
      "en": "This stage is known as the pupa stage.",
      "cn": "这个阶段它被称为“蛹”。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 16,
      "sourceSentenceId": 16,
      "chunkId": "s50-p16",
      "image": "assets/images/16.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s50-p16.mp3",
      "en": "The pupa stays shut until it finishes the transformation.",
      "cn": "蛹会一直闭合，直到完成蜕变。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 17,
      "sourceSentenceId": 17,
      "chunkId": "s50-p17",
      "image": "assets/images/17.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s50-p17.mp3",
      "en": "After a period of time, the blanket breaks and a wet, weak butterfly appears.",
      "cn": "一段时间后，“毯子”裂开，一只湿漉漉、虚弱无力的蝴蝶出现了。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 18,
      "sourceSentenceId": 18,
      "chunkId": "s50-p18",
      "image": "assets/images/18.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s50-p18.mp3",
      "en": "It may look ugly at first, but shortly, the wings fill with blood, and the beautiful, colourful butterfly spreads its wings.",
      "cn": "起初，它可能看起来有些丑，但不久后，翅膀就会充满血液，这只美丽多彩的蝴蝶就展开了它的翅膀。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 19,
      "sourceSentenceId": 19,
      "chunkId": "s50-p19",
      "image": "assets/images/19.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s50-p19.mp3",
      "en": "Now this insect can fly to the left and to the right to look for food and a partner.",
      "cn": "现在，这只昆虫可以忽左忽右地飞翔，寻找食物和配偶了。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 20,
      "sourceSentenceId": 20,
      "chunkId": "s50-p20",
      "image": "assets/images/20.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s50-p20.mp3",
      "en": "After a few weeks, this adult butterfly lays her eggs, and the cycle begins all over again.",
      "cn": "几周后，这只成年蝴蝶会产卵，于是，生命的循环再次开始。"
    }
  ]
}
